# Approval authority, by path.
#
# ADR-0007 §2.2 is the reason this file exists and the reason it is the first
# thing to get right. The W0 lane B mandate asks for eight repository classes;
# ADR-0007 implements them as directories in one repository, and §5.3 registers
# that as a deviation whose **compensating control is exactly this file** plus
# per-path pipelines and branch protection.
#
# So a path with no owner here is a path where the deviation is not compensated.
# That is the failure mode to watch for, and it is invisible: nothing breaks, a
# change merges with the wrong approver, and nobody finds out.
#
# Self-approval is prohibited wherever the governance model requires independent
# control. That is enforced by branch protection, not by this file — CODEOWNERS
# says who may approve, branch protection says that someone must.
#
# Teams are placeholders until the GitHub org has them. Replace with real teams
# before this is load-bearing; an unresolvable owner silently approves nothing
# and GitHub will not warn.

# Default: the platform lane sees anything not claimed below.
*                               @ZoikoGroup/lane-b-platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application class — trains APP and ADAPTER
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/backend/                       @ZoikoGroup/lane-d-domain
/frontend/                      @ZoikoGroup/lane-n-experience

# The fiscal kernel and the decimal runtime. Narrower than /backend/ on purpose:
# a change here can alter every tax figure the estate has ever produced, and
# ADR-0002 §5.2 names vector maintenance as content's responsibility as well as
# engineering's.
/backend/internal/domain/fiscal/ @ZoikoGroup/lane-d-domain @ZoikoGroup/lane-a-governance
/backend/testdata/golden/        @ZoikoGroup/lane-a-governance
/backend/migrations/             @ZoikoGroup/lane-d-domain @ZoikoGroup/lane-b-platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intelligence Fabric — train AI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A separate approver set from APP, which is the whole point of the AI train
# shipping on its own cadence (ADR-0006 §2.4, ADR-0007 §2.7). Lane C is named
# alongside lane L because the Gateway is an authorization component: a change
# to who may call a model is a security change, not a model change.
/intelligence/                              @ZoikoGroup/lane-l-intelligence
/intelligence/src/ztax_gateway/governance.py @ZoikoGroup/lane-l-intelligence @ZoikoGroup/lane-c-security

# The Go-side landing zone for AI outputs. ADR-0006 §2.6 forbids any conversion
# path from these types to fiscal ones, and that prohibition is easiest to erode
# by a well-meaning refactor — so it gets two approvers.
/backend/internal/domain/ai/    @ZoikoGroup/lane-l-intelligence @ZoikoGroup/lane-d-domain

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Governance
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADRs and specifications are the record of why the estate is shaped as it is.
# A change to one is a change to a decision, not to code.
/adr/                           @ZoikoGroup/lane-a-governance
/docs/specs/                    @ZoikoGroup/lane-a-governance @ZoikoGroup/lane-h-determination

# CI is where every control above is actually enforced. A change that weakens a
# gate looks like a change to a YAML file.
/.github/                       @ZoikoGroup/lane-b-platform @ZoikoGroup/lane-a-governance
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @ZoikoGroup/lane-a-governance
